# SMS — real repairs vs false work-order tickets

Ulo must not treat **status / assignment / scheduling questions** as cancelable maintenance requests — even if a mistaken ticket row exists in `maintenance_requests`.

## Rule

| Tenant message shape | Treat as |
|---|---|
| New problem report (“bedroom outlet sparking”, “sink leaking”) | Real work order — may create / update / cancel |
| Status / assignment / schedule ask (“Who is coming…?”, “What’s the status…?”, “When is my electrician coming?”) | Existing-work question — **never** a new cancelable request |

If a ticket’s **description** (first line) is clearly a status/assignment question, it is a **false work order**:

- Do **not** list it in “which request do you want to cancel?”
- Do **not** list it in “which repair are you asking about?”
- Do **not** ask the tenant to confirm cancel for it as if it were a real repair
- On cancel / “I fixed it” / “never mind”, prefer real open tickets only; close false tickets quietly in the background when cleaning up

## Examples

**False (do not offer as cancelable):**

- Who is coming to fix my electrical issue?
- What’s the status of my repair?
- When is my electrician coming?
- Did you find someone?

**Real (may offer / cancel):**

- Bedroom outlet sparking
- Kitchen sink is leaking
- AC not cooling

## Where it lives

| Concern | Module |
|---|---|
| Intent before minting a ticket | `resolveMaintenanceWorkIntent` — only `NEW_ISSUE` may create |
| Detect false ticket titles | `looksLikeStatusInquiryTicketDescription` in `inboundContextualFollowUp.ts` |
| Which-request / cancel lists | `isIdentifiableRequestLabel` + filters in `inboundInterpretationAct.ts` |
| Quiet cleanup on cancel | Close spurious inquiry tickets before handling real cancel |

## Do not

- Offer a status-question ticket as a bullet in a cancel / which-one SMS
- Mint a new work order from an assignment or status question when an open request already exists
- Rely on keyword one-offs for a single phrase — use inquiry vs problem-report shape + open-ticket context
